WEBVTT

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:06.310
Ever since he lost his wife, 
Taki-kun's been down.

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:09.250
Taki-sensei isn't dating her.

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:11.740
Honestly, in a word, it's boring.

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:14.820
She can't stand Nozomi-chan.

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:51.010
We have the performance order 
for the Kansai Competition.

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:52.620
Here we go!

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:53.380
Yeah.

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:54.750
Quiet.

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:56.760
Please don't let us be first.

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:59.640
And Kitauji High School

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:02.600
will be the sixteenth to perform.

00:02:03.610 --> 00:02:06.020
Sixteen out of twenty-three.

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:07.630
That isn't bad.

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:08.360
Yeah.

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:10.840
Um, what about the other schools—

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.190
Of the strongest schools,

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:21.040
Osaka Toushou is third in the first half. 
Shudai Fuzoku will be twelfth.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:24.160
And Myoujou Technical will be before us.

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:26.040
They're fifteenth.

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:30.330
We're after Myoujou?

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:34.030
What? You're freaking out because 
we're after a really good school?

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:36.000
Well, yeah, I mean...

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:39.330
Who cares?

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:43.680
The Kansai Competition is full of good schools.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.930
Hashimoto-sensei is correct.

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:49.220
There is no reason to worry.

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:52.150
We only need to play

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:54.560
as we always do.

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:55.270
Yes.

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:58.980
<i>We were just ten days from 
the Kansai Competition.</i>

00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:04.080
<i>I never was able to bring myself 
to talk to Nozomi-senpai</i>

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.690
<i>about what Asuka-senpai had told me.</i>

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:14.290
<i>Episode 4 
Awakening Oboe</i>

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:15.710
<b>Congrats! Kansai Concert Band Competition 
Calligraphy Performance Finals</b>

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:16.590
You'll stick around a bit longer, right?

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:17.740
Of course.

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:20.200
Yoroizuka-san, do you have a moment?

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.220
Yes.

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:25.570
I wanted to apologize to you properly.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:30.010
To be honest, when I heard your solo,

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:32.610
I felt that something was lacking.

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:36.260
Yet I decided it was good enough 
for a high school student...

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:40.990
I convinced myself there was 
a limit to your potential.

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:43.130
I'm sorry.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:45.400
Uh...

00:03:48.070 --> 00:03:50.960
It was rude of me.

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:55.040
You have incredible technique.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:56.340
But...

00:03:57.230 --> 00:03:59.960
For some reason, I feel heavy when I listen.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.630
You can have more fun.

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:07.960
Yes.

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:25.240
I'm home.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:27.180
I've made up my mind.

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:27.910
Stop!

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:31.450
Wait, Mamiko!

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:34.150
O-Onee-chan...

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:40.440
Welcome home.

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:41.510
What's wrong?

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:42.770
Oh, you know.

00:04:42.770 --> 00:04:43.880
She and Dad...

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:51.990
Why not go more all-out during this part?

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:54.140
Is that what emotion is?

00:04:56.320 --> 00:04:58.060
Good morning.

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:00.570
Morning.

00:05:02.140 --> 00:05:05.120
You probably shouldn't overthink it, either.

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:07.070
Just play however you like.

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:19.790
Kumiko...

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:23.420
I'm going to play outside.

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:27.260
<i>No...</i>

00:05:27.620 --> 00:05:29.490
<i>I have to focus.</i>

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:39.770
Okay, once more.

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:55.010
There!

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:57.070
That one went well.

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:59.010
Nice!

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:00.420
Nozomi-senpai?

00:06:02.510 --> 00:06:03.460
Morning.

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:05.110
Good morning.

00:06:05.110 --> 00:06:06.660
You're here early.

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:08.300
For Asuka-senpai?

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:09.540
Yeah.

00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:12.030
I thought I'd talk to her before practice.

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:14.720
But the Kansai Competition is coming up.

00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:18.430
I might get in the way, showing up 
before the performance.

00:06:18.430 --> 00:06:20.340
I talked to Natsuki, too.

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:23.990
I see...

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:28.280
Don't worry about it!

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:30.810
That isn't why I gave up on coming back.

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:34.580
I wish I could have helped 
Asuka-senpai, though.

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:36.080
It's a bit sad.

00:06:37.950 --> 00:06:39.390
Thanks.

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:41.210
I just wanted to say that.

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:46.590
Come to think of it, Mizore's

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:49.810
alone in the music room, isn't she?

00:06:49.810 --> 00:06:52.370
Y-Y-Yoroizuka-senpai, you mean?

00:06:52.940 --> 00:06:55.830
Yeah, I could only hear the oboe.

00:06:55.830 --> 00:06:58.530
I-Is something happening?

00:06:58.530 --> 00:06:59.140
Yeah.

00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:03.150
I heard she was told to play with more heart.

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:06.180
Apparently, she's having
difficulty with the solo.

00:07:06.910 --> 00:07:08.190
I thought it was odd...

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:12.140
That girl has a pretty
straightforward personality,

00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:14.330
but she plays very passionately.

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:16.640
She makes it sound really fun.

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:19.710
She was, like, an explosion of emotion.

00:07:20.430 --> 00:07:22.120
Really?

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:23.080
Yeah.

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:25.060
So it was bugging me.

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:27.210
I think I'll go check it out!

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:33.900
<i>Crap, crap, crap, crap!</i>

00:07:33.900 --> 00:07:34.760
<i>Oh, crap!</i>

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:37.560
Nozomi-senpai!

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:38.890
Sh-She's gone.

00:07:41.900 --> 00:07:43.060
Senpai!

00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:51.020
Nozomi-chan?

00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:57.920
Good morning.

00:07:57.920 --> 00:07:59.330
Morning.

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:00.400
Morning.

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:02.190
Bye.

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:03.230
Huh?

00:08:05.110 --> 00:08:06.350
The flute?

00:08:06.350 --> 00:08:07.090
Yeah.

00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:10.960
<i>If I'd let it go, something was 
going to happen.</i>

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:14.110
<i>I had a really bad feeling about it.</i>

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:17.960
<i>I need to do something...</i>

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:19.060
Are you sure?

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:20.420
Yeah.

00:08:20.420 --> 00:08:21.850
I'm done now.

00:08:22.380 --> 00:08:25.690
After today, I won't come by 
until the competition's over.

00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:30.190
Yeah?

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:32.190
<i>But how?</i>

00:08:36.550 --> 00:08:41.160
<i>That was when the incident occurred. 
While I was still contemplating.</i>

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:49.760
Long time, no see...

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:53.470
Mizore.

00:08:56.370 --> 00:08:57.340
Mizore!

00:08:58.460 --> 00:08:59.360
Wait...

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:00.620
Mizore!

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:06.520
Don't!

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:07.940
Yuko...

00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:12.190
Yoroizuka-senpai...

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:15.530
Damn it.

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:17.200
What do you think you're doing?

00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:20.280
Hey, what has she done?

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:21.870
She hasn't done anything.

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:23.790
That's why I'm pissed!

00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:25.160
Huh?

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:28.550
We need to find her fast.

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:34.010
Oumae-san...

00:09:35.770 --> 00:09:38.190
You know about her, don't you?

00:09:38.190 --> 00:09:40.610
Could you find Mizore for me?

00:09:40.610 --> 00:09:43.680
Right now, she has problems meeting 
people she isn't used to...

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:45.310
Please.

00:09:45.740 --> 00:09:47.470
O-Okay.

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:54.940
<i>What was going on?</i>

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:56.610
She hasn't done anything.

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:58.670
That's why I'm pissed!

00:09:58.670 --> 00:10:00.040
<i>I had no idea.</i>

00:10:00.040 --> 00:10:02.200
Oumae-san... Please.

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:03.950
Mizore!

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:07.970
<i>I had a bad feeling about what was happening.</i>

00:10:09.310 --> 00:10:10.250
I guess it's weird.

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:11.500
Thanks.

00:10:13.220 --> 00:10:16.010
<i>As we searched each classroom, one by one...</i>

00:10:17.060 --> 00:10:18.260
Mizore!

00:10:19.310 --> 00:10:20.850
Where are you?

00:10:51.280 --> 00:10:52.530
Senpai...

00:10:55.150 --> 00:10:59.460
U-Um, what happened?

00:11:00.460 --> 00:11:04.750
Uh... Do you hate Nozomi-senpai?

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:07.830
I don't hate her.

00:11:08.420 --> 00:11:09.820
That isn't it.

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:12.860
Then, did she say something?

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:14.210
No.

00:11:14.920 --> 00:11:16.090
No.

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:18.420
It isn't Nozomi's fault.

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:22.100
It's all my fault...

00:11:22.840 --> 00:11:27.750
It's because I'm afraid to see Nozomi...

00:11:29.570 --> 00:11:31.290
Why?

00:11:32.190 --> 00:11:33.750
I'll have to face...

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:36.090
reality.

00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:39.840
Reality?

00:11:43.190 --> 00:11:46.760
Nozomi is special to me.

00:11:47.700 --> 00:11:49.640
She's a precious friend.

00:11:51.250 --> 00:11:54.300
I'm bad with people.

00:11:55.780 --> 00:11:57.400
I'm gloomy.

00:11:57.400 --> 00:11:59.650
I always had trouble making friends.

00:12:00.150 --> 00:12:01.880
I was always alone.

00:12:04.900 --> 00:12:08.260
Hey, hey! Are you in any clubs, Yoroizuka-san?

00:12:09.810 --> 00:12:11.670
You're in the Go Home Club?

00:12:11.670 --> 00:12:13.540
You aren't in any clubs?

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:16.870
Despite that, Nozomi made friends with me.

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:21.560
I joined the concert band because 
Nozomi invited me.

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:20.710
<b>Club Sign-up</b>

00:12:23.250 --> 00:12:24.800
I was so happy.

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:28.060
Every day was so fun...

00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:35.310
But to Nozomi, I was just one of her friends.

00:12:36.120 --> 00:12:38.500
One of her many friends.

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:41.060
That isn't—

00:12:41.060 --> 00:12:41.900
That's why

00:12:42.660 --> 00:12:45.410
I didn't even know when she quit the club!

00:12:45.890 --> 00:12:47.410
Huh? Seriously?

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:49.260
I'm serious!

00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:55.020
Um, where's Nozomi today?

00:12:55.020 --> 00:12:55.710
Huh?

00:12:55.710 --> 00:12:56.880
She quit, of course.

00:12:58.360 --> 00:13:01.550
I was the only one who hadn't known!

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:05.540
She hadn't even talked to me about it.

00:13:05.540 --> 00:13:10.180
I was afraid to learn I'd never 
meant that much to her.

00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:11.820
I don't know.

00:13:12.650 --> 00:13:14.470
Why?

00:13:14.470 --> 00:13:18.540
I don't know why I'm in the concert band...

00:13:19.620 --> 00:13:24.430
Th-Then, why are you still playing?

00:13:25.330 --> 00:13:26.660
My instrument...

00:13:27.990 --> 00:13:33.730
My instrument is the only thing 
connecting me with Nozomi.

00:13:35.220 --> 00:13:37.480
<i>I had no words.</i>

00:13:37.950 --> 00:13:42.500
<i>To think someone would play 
music for such a reason...</i>

00:13:44.310 --> 00:13:46.510
<i>I never would have imagined it.</i>

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:52.350
Yuko-senpai.

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:53.370
Mizore...

00:13:53.750 --> 00:13:54.880
Mizore.

00:13:54.880 --> 00:13:56.340
Mizore!

00:13:56.340 --> 00:13:59.560
What are you doing? You worried me.

00:13:59.930 --> 00:14:00.940
Sorry.

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:03.940
Are you still afraid to talk to Nozomi?

00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:10.870
Nozomi is... the only one I have...

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:14.620
What if she rejects me?

00:14:15.880 --> 00:14:18.240
How can you say that?

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:21.260
So what if she does?

00:14:21.260 --> 00:14:24.090
What am I to you?!

00:14:25.970 --> 00:14:27.200
Yuko...

00:14:27.810 --> 00:14:33.770
You were nice to me because... 
you felt sorry for me...

00:14:34.470 --> 00:14:35.930
You pitied me.

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:43.760
You idiot!

00:14:43.760 --> 00:14:46.110
Are you seriously stupid?

00:14:46.300 --> 00:14:47.030
Yuko...

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:49.580
I'm going to snap before long.

00:14:49.580 --> 00:14:53.030
Why would I hang out with someone I hate?

00:14:53.030 --> 00:14:53.690
Ow.

00:14:53.690 --> 00:14:56.410
Do you think I'm that smooth?!

00:14:57.020 --> 00:14:58.210
Pity?

00:14:58.210 --> 00:14:59.170
What the hell?

00:14:59.170 --> 00:15:00.340
Senpai...

00:14:59.170 --> 00:15:02.950
You don't see me as your friend, Mizore?

00:15:02.950 --> 00:15:03.820
No...

00:15:05.220 --> 00:15:06.880
It's the same with the club!

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:10.880
You were seriously playing in 
the band <i>just</i> for Nozomi?!

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:15.850
You practiced so hard, you worked for 
the competition, and you got nothing?

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:20.360
We won in Kyoto and made it into the Kansai 
Competition, and you weren't happy?

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:23.860
I was happy!

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:25.970
I was glad I worked so hard.

00:15:25.970 --> 00:15:27.740
That my effort wasn't wasted.

00:15:28.290 --> 00:15:32.410
I felt I'd been freed from something that'd 
held me back since middle school!

00:15:32.930 --> 00:15:34.500
Didn't you, Mizore?

00:15:34.500 --> 00:15:37.290
Didn't you feel anything?

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:40.460
I was happy.

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:41.540
But...

00:15:42.590 --> 00:15:43.950
But...

00:15:43.950 --> 00:15:48.420
I felt equally guilty toward
the people who quit.

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:51.590
I didn't know if I should be happy...

00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:53.180
Of course you should!

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:02.440
Of course you should.

00:16:03.770 --> 00:16:06.820
So smile.

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:13.960
Wait, Mizore...

00:16:16.810 --> 00:16:18.410
Why are you crying?

00:16:20.760 --> 00:16:22.050
What will you do?

00:16:25.340 --> 00:16:26.540
I'll be okay.

00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:32.470
Nozomi-senpai...

00:16:33.820 --> 00:16:35.100
Nozomi!

00:16:37.150 --> 00:16:38.600
You should talk to her properly.

00:16:53.250 --> 00:16:56.570
Asuka-senpai told me I should bring this.

00:16:57.630 --> 00:17:00.950
Did I do something to upset you?

00:17:02.210 --> 00:17:04.000
I'm stupid...

00:17:04.540 --> 00:17:07.480
I honestly don't remember.

00:17:09.160 --> 00:17:10.510
Why?

00:17:12.780 --> 00:17:16.050
Why didn't you tell me?

00:17:16.510 --> 00:17:19.810
When you quit band...

00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:24.440
Because I didn't need to.

00:17:27.410 --> 00:17:30.730
You were working hard.

00:17:31.300 --> 00:17:33.440
Even when I was grumpy,

00:17:33.440 --> 00:17:37.700
even when no one was practicing, 
you were practicing by yourself.

00:17:39.090 --> 00:17:43.760
How was I supposed to ask 
you to quit with me?

00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:47.610
That's why you never told me?

00:17:48.200 --> 00:17:49.040
Yeah.

00:17:51.930 --> 00:17:55.470
Did you think I left you out?

00:17:56.770 --> 00:17:58.600
What? No!

00:17:58.600 --> 00:17:59.910
No!

00:17:59.910 --> 00:18:00.790
That so isn't it!

00:18:00.790 --> 00:18:02.300
That isn't what I...

00:18:03.050 --> 00:18:04.210
Mizore!

00:18:04.210 --> 00:18:06.260
Sorry... I'm sorry!

00:18:06.750 --> 00:18:08.150
I'm sorry.

00:18:08.150 --> 00:18:09.900
Why are you apologizing?

00:18:10.460 --> 00:18:13.250
I was avoiding you...

00:18:13.900 --> 00:18:16.030
I made a mistake...

00:18:16.450 --> 00:18:17.880
I was scared!

00:18:18.380 --> 00:18:19.810
I'm sorry.

00:18:19.810 --> 00:18:20.880
Mizore...

00:18:20.880 --> 00:18:21.990
I'm sorry.

00:18:22.450 --> 00:18:23.690
Mizore!

00:18:25.170 --> 00:18:29.580
Hey, I went to watch the Kyoto Competition.

00:18:30.450 --> 00:18:32.340
You were all spectacular.

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:34.000
I had chills.

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:37.400
I heard your solo.

00:18:38.430 --> 00:18:39.720
You were so badass.

00:18:41.080 --> 00:18:42.650
Really?

00:18:42.650 --> 00:18:44.520
Of course really.

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:50.630
Ever since middle school, I've always 
liked the way you play oboe.

00:18:57.400 --> 00:19:01.410
I get all... Like, excited inside!

00:19:01.410 --> 00:19:04.620
I want to hear you play your oboe, Mizore!

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:10.250
Mizore...

00:19:20.620 --> 00:19:23.090
I want you to hear me play, too.

00:19:32.970 --> 00:19:35.290
It sounds so pretty.

00:19:36.350 --> 00:19:38.290
I never knew she could play like that.

00:19:39.140 --> 00:19:44.530
All this time, Mizore was playing for Nozomi.

00:19:44.530 --> 00:19:45.740
I guess so.

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:49.610
I just can't compete with Nozomi.

00:19:49.610 --> 00:19:51.710
We were together for a whole year.

00:19:52.350 --> 00:19:54.900
Of course you can't.

00:19:54.900 --> 00:19:57.870
Nozomi is a hundred times 
more a good girl than you.

00:19:57.870 --> 00:19:59.010
Uh-huh.

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:01.380
Probably five hundred times more than you.

00:20:01.750 --> 00:20:05.990
But you know, I think Mizore 
was lucky she had you.

00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:11.020
Are you...

00:20:11.980 --> 00:20:14.060
trying to cheer me up?

00:20:14.060 --> 00:20:15.160
Huh?

00:20:15.160 --> 00:20:16.920
There, there. Don't be shy.

00:20:16.920 --> 00:20:17.910
What the heck?

00:20:17.910 --> 00:20:21.390
Ew, Natsuki's being nice to me!

00:20:21.390 --> 00:20:23.950
Quit being so creepy.

00:20:24.820 --> 00:20:29.120
I wanted to keep her away 
until after the competition.

00:20:29.120 --> 00:20:30.000
Sure.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:34.140
But Mizore-chan's pretty selfish, too.

00:20:34.690 --> 00:20:35.710
Don't you think?

00:20:36.220 --> 00:20:39.040
Ultimately, Mizore-chan was 
fixated on Nozomi-chan

00:20:39.040 --> 00:20:41.610
because she was afraid of being alone.

00:20:41.610 --> 00:20:44.010
Yuko-chan was insurance.

00:20:44.010 --> 00:20:45.010
No way.

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:49.810
I think people are fairly calculating 
in terms of their behavior.

00:20:51.510 --> 00:20:55.610
I think you take things too 
cynically, Asuka-senpai.

00:20:56.360 --> 00:20:57.630
Cynically, huh?

00:20:57.630 --> 00:20:58.870
Maybe so.

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:00.590
That aside...

00:21:01.980 --> 00:21:03.050
Oh.

00:21:03.050 --> 00:21:04.030
You're late.

00:21:04.030 --> 00:21:05.450
Let's head home.

00:21:05.910 --> 00:21:07.390
Okay.

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:10.040
Oumae-chan...

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:11.160
Yes?

00:21:12.160 --> 00:21:14.420
Let's make it to the Nationals.

00:21:15.200 --> 00:21:16.940
<i>When was she being honest?</i>

00:21:16.940 --> 00:21:18.790
<i>When was she putting up a front?</i>

00:21:19.330 --> 00:21:22.100
<i>It was always so hard to tell.</i>

00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:26.510
<i>It was a little scary to consider what</i>

00:21:26.510 --> 00:21:30.070
<i>she was seeing from her perspective.</i>

00:21:31.170 --> 00:21:34.250
Hey, where do you go to get so dirty?

00:21:39.170 --> 00:21:40.900
Hey, Reina...

00:21:41.740 --> 00:21:44.820
Do you play for someone in particular 
or anything like that?

00:21:45.520 --> 00:21:47.280
I've never thought about that.

00:21:49.370 --> 00:21:53.040
If I had to choose, I would say for myself.

00:21:58.040 --> 00:22:00.720
Reina, you're always so Reina...

00:22:00.720 --> 00:22:02.560
What? Are you teasing me?

00:22:02.560 --> 00:22:03.270
Not at all.

00:22:03.270 --> 00:22:05.760
<i>And the next piece begins.</i>

00:22:03.960 --> 00:22:09.970
<b>To Be Continued</b>
